From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:45:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: Register the most capable encoder first, with
 stable names

When several devices encode the same codec, the first one probed got the
plain element name (v4l2slh264enc) and the others one with the video
device node (v4l2slvideo8h264enc). The probe order is not stable: on the
RK3588 the 1080p Hantro H1 got v4l2slh264enc and the 4K VEPU580 a name
whose node number changed between boots, and as all had the same rank,
autoplugging (encodebin) chose the slower H1.

Collect the encoder devices first and register them per codec biggest
supported picture first, with a probe order independent tie break. The
first one gets the plain name and rank primary + 1. The others get one
rank less, as the VA plugin does for its secondary devices, and a name
from their driver (v4l2slhantrovpuh264enc for "hantro-vpu"), with the
bus address added when two devices share a driver
(v4l2slhantrovpufdb50000h264enc). The video device name stays the last
resort.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
